# The GHCR password. In CI the deploy workflow sets DASH_REGISTRY_PASSWORD to
# the job's GITHUB_TOKEN; locally it falls back to the gh CLI's token (dotenv
# has no ${VAR:-default}, but it does run $(...)).
DASH_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(test -n "$DASH_REGISTRY_PASSWORD" && printf %s "$DASH_REGISTRY_PASSWORD" || gh auth token)

# Rails refuses to boot in production without this, so it can never be empty.
# Same shape as above: take it from the environment when something set it,
# otherwise mint a fresh one for this deploy.
#
# The fallback is safe HERE and nowhere else: this site has no accounts, no
# sessions and no user data, so the key only signs cookies nothing reads. A
# per-deploy key means those cookies don't survive a deploy, which costs this
# site nothing. Anything with a login must set the variable instead.
#
# To make it stable, put SECRET_KEY_BASE in the repo's `docs` GitHub
# environment and thread it into the deploy step in docs-kit's reusable
# workflow (it passes SSH_PRIVATE_KEY, DEPLOY_HOST and DEPLOY_DOMAIN today);
# this line then picks it up with no change here.
SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(test -n "$SECRET_KEY_BASE" && printf %s "$SECRET_KEY_BASE" || openssl rand -hex 64)
